WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.344
Kernel update breakage is a common Linux GPU issue.

00:00:03.344 --> 00:00:06.949
A new kernel may require driver modules to be rebuilt,

00:00:06.949 --> 00:00:09.473
and missing headers can prevent that rebuild.

00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:14.159
DKMS can help, but it still depends on compatible packages and kernel headers.

00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:19.206
If a system fails after a kernel update, check the running kernel, installed headers,

00:00:19.206 --> 00:00:22.811
module build status, and driver logs before making broad changes.

00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:27.137
Secure Boot can block unsigned or improperly signed kernel modules from loading.

00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:31.102
The result may look like the driver is installed but unavailable.

00:00:31.102 --> 00:00:34.707
Some environments require module signing or Secure Boot policy changes.

00:00:34.707 --> 00:00:38.312
The right approach depends on organizational policy and system ownership.

00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:42.277
Treat this as a controlled configuration decision, not a random workaround.

00:00:42.277 --> 00:00:44.801
Display conflicts, black screens, missing device permissions,

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:49.127
and containers that cannot see the GPU each point to different layers.

00:00:49.127 --> 00:00:51.650
Display problems may involve graphics stack configuration.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:55.255
Permission problems may involve device nodes, groups, or service users.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:59.220
Container issues may involve runtime flags, toolkit configuration, or image compatibility.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.546
Version mismatch errors often indicate an unsupported combination of driver, library, runtime,

00:01:03.546 --> 00:01:04.267
and package.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:08.233
Deciding when to rollback, reinstall, or rebuild is an operational judgement.

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:11.116
Rollback is attractive when a known-good snapshot exists.

00:01:11.116 --> 00:01:16.884
Reinstall may be reasonable when the package state is confused but the base system is healthy.

00:01:16.884 --> 00:01:21.931
Rebuild may be faster when experiments have left the machine inconsistent and documentation exists.

00:01:21.931 --> 00:01:26.978
The safest troubleshooting habit is to preserve evidence, change one variable at a time,

00:01:26.978 --> 00:01:28.420
and document the result.
